    "result_text": "I implemented `publish_run` in `app/publish.py`. Both tests pass (`pytest -q`, 2 passed). Nothing was tested against the real Hub; the new test uses a fake API.\n\n**How it works:**\n1. It calls `create_repo(..., repo_type=\"dataset\", private=True, exist_ok=True)`. This creates the repo as private if it doesn't exist, and does nothing if it already does.\n2. It calls `upload_folder(...)` with the folder uploaded to the root of the repo and `ignore_patterns=[\"*.tmp\", \"wandb/*\"]`. It returns the commit URL.\n\n**Why `upload_folder` and not `upload_large_folder`:** the pinned huggingface_hub is version 2.0.0, and that version no longer has `upload_large_folder`. Its job has moved into `upload_folder`, which takes over when the `hf_xet` package is installed. `hf_xet` is a required dependency of huggingface_hub on this platform, and version 1.6.0 is already in `.venv`, so no new dependencies were needed. With it, `upload_folder`:\n- splits very large folders into several commits, so the number of files doesn't make it fail;\n- picks up where it stopped when called again after a crash: files already committed are skipped, and data already uploaded isn't sent again.\n\nThe limitation: if someone sets `HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET` or `hf_xet` is missing, it falls back to one single commit. That single commit isn't resumable and could fail on a folder this size.\n\n**Other changes:**\n- I added an optional `api` parameter, the same as `publish_summary` has, so the function can be tested with a fake.\n- I added a test in `tests/test_publish.py`. It checks the calls that are made and that the patterns keep `ckpt/model.safetensors` and `metrics.json` while dropping `*.tmp` and `wandb/...`.\n\n**Decision for you:** in huggingface_hub, `*` also matches across folders. So `*.tmp` skips temporary files at any depth, but `wandb/*` only skips the `wandb/` folder at the top of `run_dir`. If jobs can also write `wandb/` folders inside subfolders, add `\"*/wandb/*\"` to `RUN_IGNORE_PATTERNS`."
  },
